const _DC={"home_bio":"Vu Huy (b. 1999, Saigon) is a graphic and interactive designer with a focus on motion design, visual identity, and digital experience. ","info_bio":["Vu Huy (b. 1999, Saigon) is a graphic designer with a focus on visual identity, motion design, and digital experience. His work sits at the intersection of design and tech, shaped by a belief that the two disciplines are stronger together.","His practice has spanned marketing, communications, and graphic design — a range that has sharpened his instinct for what works across different mediums and audiences. He approaches each project with both analytical rigour and visual sensitivity.",""],"exp_bio":"Huy has been practicing motion design across Cavalry, After Effects, and various coding tools. There is always something new to explore, and that curiosity keeps the work honest. A few examples are shown below; the rest live on Instagram.","tools_bio":["Generative tools are one of the areas Huy is particularly interested in. The goal of this process is to further develop his own creative expression. Try it and give him feedbacks",""],"readings_bio":"Reading is one of Huy's most consistent habits. Below is his reading list, tracked from when he first started logging books on Goodreads."};
